    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47118.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "You were there. You in fact delivered one of the endorsing speeches for Kevin McCarthy. We've now run up to a situation where in the context of the debt deal and some other things where you have this relatively small caucus within the house, within even the House Republican caucus, that are still threatening to hold things up, to gum things up. It's actually been kind of remarkable to me that House Republicans have gotten as much done as they have. I was surprised that they've been able to move the ball up the field. Talk about that a little bit. How has it been governing when you have this kind of this faction within a very, very slim majority that sometimes doesn't seem that interested in governing?",
