  {
    "episode_id": 47118,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47118.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 76,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and by the way, I think it's really important to me that we don't necessarily group all of the freedom caucus or the conservatives in one group. I mean, there's different microcosms of it, but this is the only Republican majority to pass a debt ceiling bill without Democratic support. This is the only Republican majority in my lifetime to pass a border security bill without Democratic support. We've had some successes, I think, for certain people, there's a political benefit to snatching defeat from the jaws of victory. And I think some of that is how the incentive structure works. And I mean, you know, from different ways of fundraising and all of that, but we're going to keep working forward. I mean, We've got the farm bill coming up. We've got national defense authorization. We've got appropriations working. But I could tell you, if we're not unified as a Republican conference, the same thing is going to happen this time that's happened for 200 years straight. And this isn't a partisan thing. It's a chamber thing. The Senate will roll the house. I mean, that's just in the Senate's controlled by Chuck Schumer and the Democrats. So I hope my friends on all sides of the spectrum recognize that if we don't have some strategy and some sense of unity moving forward, then we're going to have real issues with whatever we pass over versus getting rolled when it comes back.",
