    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47118.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 96,
    "turn_text": "yet i i i stood on the floor of the u.s. house and warn my democratic colleagues when they censored by three-tailored green and paul gorsar i was the only republican in congress the only one that would go up to rules for two and a half hours and fight with jamie raskin on contempt orders i would like it and rob when i tell you that i was the only guy i was up there saying you cannot do these things first of all you're wrong legally Which I believe I believe I believed it then and I believe it and at least constitutionally. And second of all, there is no going back from those things. And by the way, the Biden's DOJ agreed with me on the vast majority of those content motions. So I mean, this is what happens when you continue to move those ways. So I'm just going to keep doing it. People who, I treat this stuff seriously, but I will go back to the investigations, and I think it's really important. And I did it in energy and oversight hearing the other day about the CDC buying data on U.S. citizens. We talked about the DOD earlier. We're talking about the two-tiered system of justice and how that works. And that part of it, and what the oversight committee is doing, is really, really important. You might not like the principles that were engaged, and I understand why half the country doesn't. But that Durham report is a pretty damning report on both the DOJ, but more importantly, a court system that allows for secret warrants to be given on U.S. citizens. without them ever finding out about it. And we are going to have to reauthorize 702 of FISA this year. And I'm telling you right now, anybody watching this or listening to this that thinks it's important to national security, it does not have the votes to get reauthorized, both from Democrats and Republicans. So these things have real policy consequences. But those weren't born out of Twitter. Those were born on real significant abuses of a system that is essential to Americans' constitutional rights.",
