  {
    "episode_id": 47118,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47118.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 114,
    "turn_text": "Right. I mean, I think about back in the days of Senator Conrad, Dorgan, and Pomeroy. I mean, it was the congressional delegation supporting the state party, not vice versa. Often the state party was being critical of them for voting on guns or climate change or health care or something like that, where they were probably voting with the state more than their party. And so, again, I think parties can be a nuisance for these kind of folks at high levels more than anything. I have a tough time believing, you know, I have great respect for Brent Sanford, but I think I have a tough time believing that his wife, you know, chirping on social media and taking shots at her boss didn't have anything to do with him leaving. I couldn't imagine sort of the position that put him in. But I worry, again, if we came out of this last session where I think you and I agree that there's far too much time spent on social cultural issues and not enough time on how do you pave the dam roads. This is going to accelerate that. We're going to see more trans stuff. We're going to see more book banning stuff. we're going to see more attacks on public schools. That terrifies me because I think you might see some of the more moderate, not moderate, traditional Republicans deciding not to run again because they just don't want to have to deal with the state party who's pushing them on these issues. I've",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "There has been excessive focus on social-cultural issues during the recent legislative session.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Insufficient attention has been paid to infrastructure concerns like paving dam roads.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "In the past, the congressional delegation supported the state party rather than the other way around.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
