    "turn_text": "I agree with all of that. And then I agree. And again, it's a microcosm. I think of what's coming. That's how That's how they operate. It's 100% with them or you're out. There's no room for disagreement. There's no room for nuance. It's your with them or against them. And I was trying to think if they create this legislative review committee, And let's say we're talking about representative Rob Port from from district five and my not and I vote against the book ban bill and they call me to the carpet and I got to go before this committee and explain myself I say plank three of the North Dakota Republican platform is we believe in limited government. I believe that that usurping that we already have local library boards who can handle this stuff. I think creating a statewide law is big government reaching down and usurping from local government. Tell me I'm wrong. There's no room for that nuance in the party anymore where I say this is a book ban. I don't think this is right. I think this is big government. I'm not allowed in the Republican party. If the Republican party doesn't have room for that kind of nuance, it's going to be a smaller party and a smaller Republican party means a bigger Democratic party. Is that what they want?",
