    "turn_text": "So, Rob, I think, you know, in thinking about the logical next step on this North Dakota right to life thing is if the Magrams, the Hoversins, those people are upset that they didn't get 100% and North Dakota right to life agreed with that, that they should change their scorecard. Does that mean Senator Murdall and Senator Cleary and Senator Deaver, who did have 100% on the scorecard, did they do something wrong? According to the North Dakota Right to Life board, who fired all these staff people, because I would suggest the Murdals, Clearies, Devers, and those folks that were at 100%, actually were living and voting their values and the values of their faith in what's good for children in this country. It's very frustrating, but it is a microcosm, like you said, of sort of if you're not 100% with us, we're gonna fire you or not renew your contracts.",
