    "turn_idx": 186,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, or, or, or, you know, we're going to call you before our legislative review committee or, you know, we're going to call for a primary challenger to you or whatever. And, you know, it's going to be interesting to see what happens with some of the money, um, how, you know, You know, and also because it's an open process. If somebody, I mean, if you're, I mean, there's going to be a lot of lawmakers who are going to feel left out in the cold. There's going to be some statewides to feel left out in the cold. How hard is it for them to file some paperwork, start a multi candidate pack, create a landing place for some of that money that would have gone to the party. and just filter it straight to campaigns, and filter it straight to candidates who say, I'm just going to skip the convention and go right to the June primary. In the short term, that's probably a good path for the normies. I think it's one way that will demonstrate that these folks now in charge of the party have a lot less power than they think they do. But long term, what does that mean for the Republican Party and its ability to you know, organize candidates and everything else in the future. Because it's in the short term, again, a lot of the state-wise and stuff can get away with it. But eventually, if this continues, the party's going to deteriorate.",
